# Go Conventions

Apply when editing Go sources (exclude `*_test.go` for app logic reviews). Read [doc/stack.md](../../doc/stack.md). Subagent: `build-agent`.

## Layout

Follow `layout` in `doc/stack.md` (`cmd/`, `internal/`, etc.).

## Style

- Small packages and functions
- Explicit error handling
- Match existing project patterns

## Naming

Full rules: [doc/coding-conventions.md](../../doc/coding-conventions.md). Follow Effective Go.

| Target | Case | Example |
|--------|------|---------|
| Unexported identifiers | lowerCamelCase | `userName`, `fetchOrder` |
| Exported identifiers | PascalCase | `UserName`, `FetchOrder` |
| Files | snake_case | `user_service.go` |
| Test functions | `TestTCNNN_<What>` | `TestTC001_Returns404WhenMissing` |

Semantics: verb-first functions; `is`/`has`/`can` booleans; plural collections; English identifiers; comments may be Japanese.

## Before finishing

Use `test_all` from `doc/stack.md` (`go test ./...`, `go vet`).
